Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/vishvananda/netlink v1.3.1

XfrmState gains AFUnspec, which sets XFRM_STATE_AF_UNSPEC in
xfrm_usersa_info.flags and is read back from it. Upstream sets no flag but
ESN, so a tunnel-mode state installed with no selector reaches the kernel's
copy_from_user_state (net/xfrm/xfrm_user.c), where "if (!x->sel.family &&
!(p->flags & XFRM_STATE_AF_UNSPEC)) x->sel.family = p->family;" gives the
selector the outer family, and xfrm_state_look_at then skips the state for a
flow of the other inner family. RFC 4301 Section 5.1.2: "IPsec allows the
IP version of the encapsulating header to be different from that of the
inner header."

Its test, TestXfrmStateAFUnspecFlag in xfrm_state_af_unspec_linux_test.go,
checks the flag value written and read back.

No upstream pull request is opened yet for this change.

Needs netlink-xfrm-01-state-readback-esn-replay.patch: the line that
reads the flag back follows the ESN line that patch adds.

Applies unchanged to upstream main (e0e26cd, 2026-11-13) after the patches it
needs, not on its own, and its test passes there unprivileged.

Delete this patch when go.mod requires an upstream release that contains the
change.

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_af_unspec_linux_test.go b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_af_unspec_linux_test.go
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_af_unspec_linux_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+package netlink
+
+import (
+	"testing"
+
+	"github.com/vishvananda/netlink/nl"
+)
+
+// TestXfrmStateAFUnspecFlag checks that AFUnspec sets XFRM_STATE_AF_UNSPEC, which is
+// 0x20 in include/uapi/linux/xfrm.h, and is read back from it.
+func TestXfrmStateAFUnspecFlag(t *testing.T) {
+	if got := xfrmUsersaInfoFromXfrmState(&XfrmState{AFUnspec: true}).Flags; got != 0x20 {
+		t.Errorf("flags with AFUnspec = %#x, want 0x20", got)
+	}
+	if got := xfrmUsersaInfoFromXfrmState(&XfrmState{}).Flags; got != 0 {
+		t.Errorf("flags without AFUnspec = %#x, want 0", got)
+	}
+	if !xfrmStateFromXfrmUsersaInfo(&nl.XfrmUsersaInfo{Flags: 0x20}).AFUnspec {
+		t.Errorf("AFUnspec = false for flags 0x20, want true")
+	}
+	if xfrmStateFromXfrmUsersaInfo(&nl.XfrmUsersaInfo{}).AFUnspec {
+		t.Errorf("AFUnspec = true for flags 0, want false")
+	}
+}
diff --git a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
--- a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_state_linux.go
